0..69 Comment "/// This source states a list flow whose translator visits each cell."
70..73 Comment "///"
74..151 Comment "/// The translator swaps one record and rides the record flow through a list."
152..216 Comment "/// Each list cell uses the translated head and translated tail."
217..220 Comment "///"
221..270 Comment "/// The list flow uses that recursive translator."
271..325 Comment "/// The checker rides source lists through the result."
326..405 Comment "/// At each cell, the image binds the translator\'s image of the rigid tail, and"
406..468 Comment "/// it is natural. So the translator is natural at every list."
469..472 Comment "///"
473..552 Comment "/// - cites: [Gratzer-2026-directed_univalence_simplicial_homotopy_type_theory]"
